# Responsive Web Design & Media Queries

Responsive design adapts UI to device capabilities. This topic walks through a mobile-first strategy and practical breakpoints, plus fluid units for resilient layouts.

Mobile-first approach:
- Start with base (mobile) styles and layer media queries for larger screens.

Breakpoints and examples:
```css
:root { --container-padding: 1rem; }
@media (min-width: 640px) { :root { --container-padding: 1.25rem; } }
@media (min-width: 1024px) { .grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); } }
```

Responsive images:
- Use srcset and sizes to deliver appropriate image resolutions.

Testing and performance:
- Test across multiple viewports and emulate slow networks to ensure UX holds.

Key takeaways:
- Prefer fluid units and CSS layout primitives over pixel hacks.
